
# 🌡️ THERMORA – Temperature Converter

A creative, modern and interactive temperature conversion website developed using HTML5, CSS3 and Vanilla JavaScript.

## ✨ Project Overview

THERMORA is a responsive temperature converter that allows users to convert values between Celsius, Fahrenheit and Kelvin.

The website features a unique Fire & Ice inspired design with glowing visual effects, glassmorphism UI components and interactive temperature conversion.

## 🚀 Features

- Convert Celsius, Fahrenheit and Kelvin.
- Display all three converted results simultaneously.
- Real-time numeric input validation.
- Absolute zero validation for all three temperature scales.
- User-friendly error messages.
- Interactive Convert and Clear buttons.
- Dynamic temperature unit symbols.
- Light and dark theme toggle.
- Responsive mobile navigation.
- Animated Fire & Ice visual elements.
- Responsive desktop, tablet and mobile layout.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript

## 🧮 Conversion Formulas

**Celsius to Fahrenheit**

°F = (°C × 9/5) + 32

**Fahrenheit to Celsius**

°C = (°F − 32) × 5/9

**Celsius to Kelvin**

K = °C + 273.15

**Kelvin to Celsius**

°C = K − 273.15

## 🌡️ Absolute Zero Validation

The application validates the minimum temperature limits:

| Temperature Scale | Absolute Zero |
|---|---:|
| Celsius | -273.15 °C |
| Fahrenheit | -459.67 °F |
| Kelvin | 0 K |

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
WebDev-L1-TemperatureConverter/
│
